<urn:atm:triage:finding/AJ-FINAL-008-ARCH-DOC-EVIDENCE-GAP>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AJ-FINAL-008-ARCH-DOC-EVIDENCE-GAP" ;
  triage:title "docs/architecture.md Section 21.6.3 was not reconciled to the same clause-level evidence standard as AJ.9's other 3 governing docs" ;
  triage:description "AJ.9's reconciliation brought docs/requirements.md, docs/adr/ADR-045-runtime-observation-attribution.md, and docs/team-member-state.md up to a clause-level source-symbol/test-name evidence standard (see ADR-045's 16-row Implementation evidence table). docs/architecture.md Section 21.6.3 (Doctor Health Interface, lines ~3038-3078) accurately describes the runtime-observation boundary conceptually (non-authoritative telemetry, closed ingress set, no IdentityConflict lifecycle state) but carries no source-symbol/test-name citations and no explicit cross-reference to ADR-045 or team-member-state.md, unlike its sibling docs. Content is not false, so this is a completeness gap rather than a false-claim regression -- but the Phase Exit Criteria checkbox 'AJ.9 requirements, ADR, architecture, and team-member-state agree with the merged implementation' implies architecture.md was reconciled to the same rigor as the other three. Found by req-qa during Phase AJ's final holistic gate review. QA source: PR #759." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AJ" ;
